<title>HONG KONG: Continental interim profit jumps sharply.</title>
<headline>Continental interim profit jumps sharply.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   9.0   vs 3.9</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    nil   vs nil</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  nil   vs 2.2 loss</p>
<p>    Net			    20.5  vs 8.8</p>
<p>    Turnover		     312.9 vs 248.7</p>
<p>    Company name		 Continental Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  N/A</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   N/A</p>
<p>NOTE - Continental Holdings designs and manufactures jewellery for export. The exceptional item for the comparison represents a specific provision made for balances due from an Australian customer which was under receivership.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
